WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.935
Vinnie and Mandy froze with fear.

2
00:00:06.936 --> 00:00:11.071
All the sailors stopped rowing or woke up.

3
00:00:11.072 --> 00:00:13.674
They stared at the children.

4
00:00:13.675 --> 00:00:17.873
The large man walked over to Vinnie and Mandy.

5
00:00:17.874 --> 00:00:21.675
Mandy guessed he was the captain.

6
00:00:21.676 --> 00:00:28.492
"Gunnar! Explain! Who are they?" the captain asked the fair boy.

7
00:00:28.493 --> 00:00:32.400
"Sir, I don’t know," the boy replied.

8
00:00:32.401 --> 00:00:34.541
"Why did you hide here?

9
00:00:34.542 --> 00:00:37.545
Do you want to be warriors like Gunnar?"

10
00:00:37.546 --> 00:00:42.449
The captain pointed his sword at Vinnie and Mandy.

11
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.145
"Yes, sir!" Vinnie shouted.

12
00:00:45.146 --> 00:00:49.933
"Ah, true Viking spirit!" the captain said.

13
00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:52.815
"I like your courage, boy."

14
00:00:52.816 --> 00:00:56.534
The captain slapped Vinnie on the back.

15
00:00:56.535 --> 00:00:59.937
Vinnie nearly fell over.

16
00:00:59.938 --> 00:01:03.549
The captain stopped and glared at Mandy.

17
00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:08.667
"But you! Little girls should not be sneaking onto a Viking ship.

18
00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:12.546
Especially one as weak as you," he sneered.

19
00:01:12.547 --> 00:01:16.139
Mandy threw back her head proudly.

20
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:22.014
"I may look weak, sir," she replied in a clear, loud voice.

21
00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:25.119
"But I am as strong as a horse."

22
00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.409
"Land ho!" the lookout shouted.

23
00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:32.212
"Finally!" the captain said.

24
00:01:32.213 --> 00:01:34.669
"Get ready to go ashore."

25
00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:37.947
Turning to Vinnie and Mandy, he said,

26
00:01:37.948 --> 00:01:41.933
"You two—stay with Gunnar."

27
00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:47.228
Mandy let out a sigh of relief as the captain turned away.

28
00:01:47.229 --> 00:01:53.068
"Vinnie! I don’t think he likes me being on the ship," she said.

29
00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:57.954
"Don’t worry. You were really brave," Vinnie replied.

30
00:01:57.955 --> 00:02:00.134
He turned to Gunnar. "Where

31
00:02:00.135 --> 00:02:03.696
are we going?" he asked. "This

32
00:02:03.697 --> 00:02:06.268
port is Kaupang. It

33
00:02:06.269 --> 00:02:12.678
is a Viking village where we trade and sell our goods," Gunnar said proudly. "The

34
00:02:12.679 --> 00:02:15.760
captain is the best bear hunter! He

35
00:02:15.761 --> 00:02:19.935
brought bear skins from our village in the icy North." "Here

36
00:02:19.936 --> 00:02:23.133
we go, Vinnie. Look!" Mandy

37
00:02:23.134 --> 00:02:26.750
grabbed his arm. The

38
00:02:26.751 --> 00:02:31.149
Sleeping Dragon pulled smoothly into port. Several

39
00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.860
other Viking ships were already docked there. Each

40
00:02:35.861 --> 00:02:38.952
ship was long and slender. Viking

41
00:02:38.953 --> 00:02:43.938
sailors carried large chests out of the ships. Some

42
00:02:43.939 --> 00:02:48.676
carried smaller boxes of jewelry. "Gunnar!"

43
00:02:48.677 --> 00:02:52.003
the captain called out. "Take

44
00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:55.943
this to Old Dirk, the blacksmith." The

45
00:02:55.944 --> 00:03:00.437
captain handed Gunnar a jewelry box. "Tell

46
00:03:00.438 --> 00:03:02.615
him I sent you. He

47
00:03:02.616 --> 00:03:05.006
will know what to do." "Yes,

48
00:03:05.007 --> 00:03:09.608
captain," said Gunnar as he took the box. "Do

49
00:03:09.609 --> 00:03:13.948
not disappoint me," the captain roared. "And

50
00:03:13.949 --> 00:03:16.916
keep an eye on those two." He

51
00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:19.429
pointed to Vinnie and Mandy. "Come

52
00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:22.486
on!" Gunnar called. Vinnie

53
00:03:22.487 --> 00:03:27.337
and Mandy followed him off the Sleeping Dragon .

54
00:03:27.338 --> 00:03:31.140
Kaupang was a busy open market.

55
00:03:31.141 --> 00:03:35.333
People exchanged furs for iron weapons.

56
00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:42.266
Others bought bear skins, walrus tusks, and whale bones with silver coins.

57
00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:47.533
Finally the children arrived at the blacksmith’s workshop.

58
00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:51.404
The boy introduced himself to the blacksmith.

59
00:03:51.405 --> 00:03:55.944
"I am Gunnar. Captain Skull-Crusher sent me."

60
00:03:55.945 --> 00:03:59.145
Vinnie and Mandy stared at each other.

61
00:03:59.146 --> 00:04:06.300
"Skull-Crusher?" they gasped.

